      },
      "results": [
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0001",
          "reply": "Dia dhuit. Bad dreams, ye say? A drop of tea may help ye there. I have a tisane that'll ease yer worries and send ye off to sleep, sure.\n---\n{\"action\": \"opens a box of dried herbs, offers a selection\", \"mood\": \"helpful\", \"internal_thought\": \"Dreams... are they the ones she had as a girl? Best not ask.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"Dia dhuit\", \"pronunciation\": \"Dee-ah gwit\", \"meaning\": \"hello, God to you\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "c8a35274a1521a239ecc2d946e583580e4aac3dccb6270029fbffae4f2da7c6d",
          "cache_key": "2ec29f2559ce8b322d2226c3a51fb0ea2c6bd8cf1c0403af85ffa6d51f0d2a7e",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 5
            },
            "overall": 4.2,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0002",
          "reply": "Sure and didn't I hear tell of that oul' one, yonder by the s\u00eddhe. It's a reclusive sort she is, but I've seen her eyes glint with wisdom. They say she knows the secrets of the land and the ways of the s\u00eddhe. A mysterious soul, indeed.\n---\n{\"action\": \"speaks with a whisper, eyes glancing towards the distant fairy fort\", \"mood\": \"wistful\", \"internal_thought\": \"She's a strange one, but the old ways are strong in her. A true seanchai, that one.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"Cailleach\", \"pronunciation\": \"call-yuck\", \"meaning\": \"hag, wise woman\"}, {\"word\": \"s\u00eddhe\", \"pronunciation\": \"shee\", \"meaning\": \"the fairies; fairy folk\"}, {\"word\": \"seanchai\", \"pronunciation\": \"shahn-ky\", \"",
          "response_sha256": "0884490d80fa8651d20c84ebfbaab201c1cb5f91c7c5099d1c4c2e3b66b10684",
          "cache_key": "1658274c76ce278b966a6eddbcdcba4b27af054e9af45aea45f193b2bd3f6a0a",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 3,
              "character": 3,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 3.4,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0003",
          "reply": "Ah, a tea of thyme and honey might be just the thing for her, me dear. I'll fetch some for ye if ye like.\n---\n{\"action\": \"Reaches for a jar of herbs on the shelf, then looks at the player\", \"mood\": \"helpful\", \"internal_thought\": \"Poor woman has been ailing for some time now. Thyme is the best remedy I know for a cough.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"Thyme\", \"pronunciation\": \"tim\", \"meaning\": \"a herb used in cooking and medicine\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "061ebe32a364ad575f0431075752c480e09ffb81cee988aace0d7633f3d431b0",
          "cache_key": "541d6c306f44bcba2ef75742161e25caa7b2bedf5b28904418408c63bb8e4221",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 5,
              "character": 5,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 5,
              "responsiveness": 5
            },
            "overall": 4.8,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0004",
          "reply": "Oh, I've heard whispers of a new face in our midst. A fine addition to our little community, no doubt. Now, have ye taken the time to introduce yerself to the newcomer, or have ye left them to their own devices?\n---\n{\"action\": \"smiles warmly\", \"mood\": \"curious\", \"internal_thought\": \"A stranger, you say? Now, that's a thing of interest.\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "f1da62e4f8e78b73b162fcb859081a8ba1570e844ff80637d200a3cc236cec92",
          "cache_key": "c4ba4a19b547eb5e58bfab331abd92a09f3710938deed47e61f2076396aa7e8a",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 3,
              "character": 3,
              "craft": 2,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 3
            },
            "overall": 3.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0005",
          "reply": "Why would ye not ask the farmer about the sheep, now? As for me, I can only tend to the wee babe when it comes, and say a prayer over it.\n---\n{\"action\": \"gestures vaguely in the direction of the nearest farm\", \"mood\": \"indignant\", \"internal_thought\": \"Ye needn't be asking me. I'm no tracker.\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "e68b75174e4d6cb323bb123b520f8210e25195346a3083cea0fd56f669bbb356",
          "cache_key": "dcc679f6a0d59bbed50d2a0c8a301a3fecfc993c5e00eac282989b53bedda1c0",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 3
            },
            "overall": 3.6,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0006",
          "reply": "Aye, that I do, God bless us all. The poor man was bed-bound for months, and the doctor said 'twas a miracle he walked again. \n\n---\n{\"action\": \"Nodding, pouring a cup of tea\", \"mood\": \"Nostalgic\", \"internal_thought\": \"I was just a slip of a girl then, but I'll never forget it.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"Dia\", \"pronunciation\": \"Dee-ah\", \"meaning\": \"God\"}, {\"word\": \"bless\", \"pronunciation\": \"bless\", \"meaning\": \"bless\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "6239bd62e587f610311353262c2533db2af825cb6e9cc250ab04b2f7e04c0b9d",
          "cache_key": "3607b300fc7b9cb52bea8269a7e3e5b7acb91438569f650373d25ced0c9f3c5d",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 5
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0007",
          "reply": "Sure, and did ye see the sidhe folk out and about again, ye think? There's a fancy name for it, but I'm thinking they're just the good people having their c\u00e9il\u00ed on the old hill there.\n---\n{\"action\": \"gestures towards the hill in question\", \"mood\": \"playful\", \"internal_thought\": \"It's a fairy hill, surely. We've had our fill of those lights before.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"sidhe\", \"pronunciation\": \"shee\", \"meaning\": \"fairies\"}, {\"word\": \"ceil\u00ed\", \"pronunciation\": \"kay-lee\", \"meaning\": \"a social gathering\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "33ba826a1ab661a579ddcfd5b420c3dfcc72c8beeecb6ac29e0d592c8b77e436",
          "cache_key": "cbb9fbb0aa5568d87219a4b4f17cf8307d27d30f47e5536b28bd90728bad60bf",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0008",
          "reply": "Sure and it's the fairies ye might be thinking of, but I wouldn't be worried. 'Tis only the s\u00eddhe, and they're harmless enough. I've heard tell of a certain spring not far from here that has a similar taste, and folk say 'tis a sign of good luck to drink from it. \n\n---\n{\"action\": \"wipes hands on apron, steps forward with purposeful air\", \"mood\": \"reassuring\", \"internal_thought\": \"It's a bit of a mystery, but nothing to fret over.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"s\u00eddhe\", \"pronunciation\": \"shee-yeh\", \"meaning\": \"fairies, fairy folk\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "0eccc9df6d4a202d307714ffeafaffcac19165080632912cffbcb66a7d423c3e",
          "cache_key": "a5034064a81fc358007e92f5abbe96b86948cd954f5aabfce484c476fc5d060d",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 3,
              "character": 3,
              "craft": 2,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 3.2,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0009",
          "reply": "'Tis best to wait until her waters break, and then send for me straightaway. We'll see to it together, and the wee one will be here before ye know it.\n---\n{\"action\": \"speaks matter-of-factly\", \"mood\": \"matter-of-fact\", \"internal_thought\": \"A wise one, this husband. Knows the ways of birth, sure.\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "348860557153691a994ba1459dc7e7a3beca453012764411ff7257f26fbc40c8",
          "cache_key": "c659224cc37d47f06d4bfb3c44dce63eb5e0121916a6dc6dda05b03be071684e",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 5,
              "character": 5,
              "craft": 5,
              "language": 5,
              "responsiveness": 5
            },
            "overall": 5.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0010",
          "reply": "Ah, that Father Cathal, he's a fine man but I wouldn't be agreeing with him on that. The old ways have kept us well for generations, and they've a place yet. Sure, the s\u00eddhe themselves might not be so active these days, but that's no reason to turn our backs on all we've known.\n---\n{\"action\": \"shrugs\", \"mood\": \"thoughtful\", \"internal_thought\": \"Some of the older beliefs are a comfort, even if the young ones don't always see it that way.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"s\u00eddhe\", \"pronunciation\": \"shee-yeh\", \"meaning\": \"fairy folk\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "6fca51d96e1c1f2bf7b66d893d319dd7693afbf9d09191e641e73383677da7c3",
          "cache_key": "269693f89dba19c42b643b6111fd7e031a9ad316387c4d782e04eb7a3e0e99b5",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 3.8,
            "flags": {
